PARTIAL / INTERNAL / FULL-REGRESSION-TEST-GATED

CONTRACT
One local Core process owns Repository, MetadataStore/SQLite, CAS, Workspace
filesystem mutation, Operation lifecycle, and recovery entry. Multiple local
Runtime processes use ephemeral sessions to send unchanged external Agent
protocol v1.0 requests. Runtime Session is not Agent, Execution, Operation, or
durable state. Durable Operation.session_id was not repurposed.

IMPLEMENTATION BOUNDARY
The multi-session broker is a test-only filesystem multiplexing harness. The
production JSONL process remains one attached stdin/stdout stream and is not a
multi-client daemon. No HTTP, MCP, remote sync, durable session table, provider
adapter, authentication service, or protocol v1.0 change was introduced.

REAL-PROCESS SCENARIOS
- three Runtime processes with distinct Agents, Tasks, and Executions: PASS
- same Agent across multiple Runtime processes and Executions: PASS
- same Execution across two Runtime processes: PASS
- distinct concurrent Operations: PASS
- one lifecycle winner and one stale REVISION_CONFLICT: PASS
- Runtime exits after request publication without reading response: PASS
- another session resolves the durable Operation: PASS
- invalidated session rejects later requests: PASS
- graceful stop drains queued request and rejects new connection: PASS
- started Operation remains started and is not falsely completed: PASS
- forced Core termination and owner release: PASS
- replacement Core cold reopen and Runtime reconnect: PASS

